# Git-ignored paths symlinked from the main tree into every new worktree.
#
# `git worktree add` materializes only tracked files, so a fresh worktree starts without
# these, and the failure is silent: the session works without the file and never learns
# it existed. Anything created at one of these paths inside a worktree is also deleted
# with the worktree, without a warning, because ignored paths are excluded from git's
# "worktree is dirty" check. A symlink prevents both.
#
# One path per line. `#` comments and blank lines are ignored. A path that does not
# exist in the main tree is skipped, so listing an optional one costs nothing.
local
.beads
.ai-jail
.env
